CVE-2026-41225 is listed for BIG-IP only, in 21.0.0 before version 21.0.0.2, 17.5.0 before version 17.5.1.6 and 17.1.0 before version 17.1.3.2, with the 16.1 branch past end of technical support and not evaluated ([ENISA EUVD-2026-29986](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/enisa/eu_vulnerability_database/EUVD-2026-29986)); F5 published it on 2026-05-13 ([SecurityWeek, 2026-05-14](https://www.securityweek.com/f5-patches-over-50-vulnerabilities/)). The prerequisite is an authenticated account with at least the Manager role and network access to iControl REST through the management port or a self IP address, and F5 says there is no data-plane exposure ([SecurityWeek, 2026-05-14](https://www.securityweek.com/f5-patches-over-50-vulnerabilities/)); no source describes a credential-theft chain, a European public-sector deployment base or monitoring guidance. The secondary list of CVE ids grouped by flaw class did not match NCSC-NL's advisory ([NCSC-NL NCSC-2026-0162, 2026-05-15](https://advisories.ncsc.nl/csaf/v2/2026/ncsc-2026-0162.json)) and is dropped. F5's own score is CVSS 4.0 8.6 ([ENISA EUVD-2026-29986](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/enisa/eu_vulnerability_database/EUVD-2026-29986)); the 9.1 comes from NCSC-NL as a CVSS 3.1 score with a changed scope ([NCSC-NL NCSC-2026-0162, 2026-05-15](https://advisories.ncsc.nl/csaf/v2/2026/ncsc-2026-0162.json)).
